{"name":"Natural Harmony","hex":"#91aa90","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"natural","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Existing in nature.","Normally associated with a particular person or thing; inherently related to the nature of a thing or creature."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native inhabitant of a place, country, etc.","A note that is not or is no longer to be modified by an accidental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/natural"},{"term":"harmony","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Agreement or accord.","A pleasing combination of elements, or arrangement of sounds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harmony"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harmony","blocks":[{"text":"In music, harmony is the concept of combining different sounds in order to create new, distinct musical ideas. Theories of harmony seek to describe or explain the effects created by distinct pitches or tones coinciding with one another; harmonic objects such as chords, textures and tonalities are identified, defined, and categorized in the development of these theories. Harmony is broadly understood to involve both a \"vertical\" dimension (frequency-space) and a \"horizontal\" dimension (time-space), and often overlaps with related musical concepts such as melody, timbre, and form."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg/330px-US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harmony"},{"title":"Harmony (color)","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, color harmony is a property of certain aesthetically pleasing color combinations. These combinations create pleasing contrasts and consonances that are said to be harmonious. These combinations can be of complementary colors, split-complementary colors, color triads, or analogous colors. Color harmony has been a topic of extensive study throughout history, but only since the Renaissance and the Scientific Revolution has it seen extensive codification. Artists and designers make use of these harmonies in order to achieve certain moods or aesthetics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harmony_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg/500px-US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg/1280px-US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg/500px-US_Navy_080615-N-7656R-003_Navy_Band_Northwest%27s_Barbershop_Quartet_win_the_hearts_of_the_audience_with_a_John_Philip_Sousa_rendition_of.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Barbershop quartets, such as this US Navy Band ensemble, sing four-part pieces, made up of a melody line (normally the lead) and three harmony parts. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki